<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Settings for the Drone Automation modules. Debug="1" logs (throttled) why each module is or
  isn't acting; set Debug="0" to silence once things work.

  Shared knobs (per module section):
    SpeedMultiplier     scales simulated action time. 0.5 = twice as fast.
    MaxCatchupSeconds   ceiling on banked seconds, so reloads cannot burst.
    VerticalRadius      vertical reach.

  LEVELS: every reach/time value below is the Quality 6 (top-tier) ceiling. A module's installed
  Quality (1-6) scales it toward the Q1 floor via two knobs per section:
    LowQualityReach     Q1 reach as a fraction of the configured reach (0..1). Q6 = full.
    LowQualityTimeMult  Q1 action time as a multiple of the configured time (>=1). Q6 = full speed.
  Crafted quality follows your Robotics crafting skill (Q1 below Robotics 80, up to Q6 at 100);
  traders roll their own. Loot never drops a module, only its schematic.

  PARKING: tell the drone to hold position with the vanilla "stay" command and the block modules
  work the ground around the spot you parked it on, instead of around you. Its owner still has to be
  online, but no longer has to be standing there - so a drone parked in the farm keeps reaping while
  you're out looting. Auto-Loot always works around the drone itself.
    WorkWhileParked   0 = a parked drone idles instead (the old behaviour).
    MaxOwnerDistance  how far a FOLLOWING drone may be from its owner and still work blocks, in
                      metres (0 disables the check). A following drone is normally right beside you,
                      so this only catches one that's been left behind. Parked drones are exempt -
                      working away from you is the whole point of parking one.
-->
<droneautomation Debug="0" WorkWhileParked="1" MaxOwnerDistance="25">
	<!--
	  Auto-Loot: open bags/containers, grab dropped items, into the drone's bag.
	    Radius              horizontal metres for block containers. 0 = bags and dropped items only.
	    EntityRadius        horizontal metres for loot bags and dropped items.
	    MinSecondsPerTarget floor per target.
	    ItemPickupSeconds   charged per loose ground item.
	    SkipIfPlayerWithin  skip targets within this many metres of any online player. 0 disables.
	    ThrownGraceSeconds  how long anything you THREW is left alone. A thrown rock, molotov or
	                        grenade is a normal dropped item as far as the game is concerned, so
	                        without this the drone can pick one up in mid-air. Live explosives and
	                        items still in flight are always skipped, whatever this is set to; the
	                        grace period is what leaves a thrown rock long enough to pull a zombie.
	-->
	<autoLoot Radius="8"
	          EntityRadius="15"
	          VerticalRadius="6"
	          SpeedMultiplier="1"
	          MinSecondsPerTarget="0.25"
	          ItemPickupSeconds="0.25"
	          MaxCatchupSeconds="5"
	          SkipIfPlayerWithin="0"
	          ThrownGraceSeconds="5"
	          LowQualityReach="0.55"
	          LowQualityTimeMult="2" />

	<!--
	  Auto-Salvage: wrench salvageable blocks (cars, sinks, machines) into the drone's bag.
	  Destructive, so it only touches UNCLAIMED ground - never inside anyone's land claim, yours
	  included, and that rule has no setting because there is no safe way to switch it off.
	  Trader areas are ALWAYS off limits and cannot be enabled (the game reports a trader area as
	  unclaimed, so the land-claim rule alone would happily let the drone strip the trader).

	  WHAT it takes is each player's own choice, made in game: talk to the drone > Automation
	  modules > Auto-Salvage, and switch on the kinds of thing it may take (vehicles,
	  appliances, lights, sinks/toilets/pipes, furniture/decor/signs, emptied containers, everything
	  else). It starts with NOTHING picked, and says so the first time it passes something by. Players
	  fine-tune by name with /das (skip one kind inside a picked group, or allow one outside it), and
	  those rules are per player too - one player's /das never changes anyone else's drone.
	    Radius / VerticalRadius   reach. Kept small by default because it destroys blocks.
	    SecondsPerStep            charged per downgrade step (one wrench swing); a car takes several.
	    SalvageWorkstations       1 = also scrap forges, workbenches, campfires, chem stations and
	                              cement mixers. Off by default: they're things you use, and one may
	                              still hold your materials.
	    SalvageInPOIs             0 = never wrench anything inside a POI's footprint. On by default,
	                              because stripping cars and sinks as you clear a building is the
	                              whole point of the module.
	    SalvageVendingMachines    1 = also scrap WORKING vending machines - the ones you can still
	                              buy from, and the ones a player can rent and stock. Off by default:
	                              a working machine is a shop, not scrap. Their broken shells stay
	                              salvageable whatever this is set to.
	    CountAsHoldingSalvageTool 1 = the drone counts as holding a wrench while it works out what a
	                              block pays. Vanilla gates some salvage bonuses on you HOLDING a
	                              salvage tool - Hacker's candy and the Scavenger Gloves - so without
	                              this the drone only got them in the accident where you happened to
	                              have your wrench out, and never if you were holding a gun. The
	                              Salvage Operations perk is not gated and applies either way.
	    SalvageToolTags           the tags that pretence claims. Vanilla's wrench, ratchet and impact
	                              driver carry all three; only worth changing under an overhaul that
	                              renames them.
	    HeatMultiplier            heat (screamer) made per broken stage, as a multiple of what
	                              breaking that stage by hand makes. 1 = the same heat as wrenching
	                              it yourself, so the drone draws screamers like you do; 0 = silent,
	                              the way versions before 0.9.0 were.
	    SalvageSwitches           1 = also scrap switches, buttons, valve handles, key racks, wire
	                              and timer relays, pressure plates, quest generators and powered
	                              doors, lights and traps. Off by default, and leave it off: these
	                              are what open a POI's doors, they cannot be crafted or looted
	                              back, and wrenching one breaks that POI for the life of the save.
	    ChatPrefix                the chat command players use to see and change their own rules.
	    StartTargets              what a player has picked before they open the menu: "none" (the
	                              default - the drone takes nothing until its owner chooses) or
	                              "all", which switches every group on once per player, the way
	                              versions before 0.12 behaved. A player who then switches groups
	                              off keeps them off.
	    NewTargetPolicy           inside the groups a player picked, what to do with a kind of block
	                              their drone has never salvaged: "allow" wrenches it and says so
	                              once, "ask" leaves it standing until they run /das allow.
	    AnnounceNewTargets        0 = never speak up. Left on, the drone says once per kind of block
	                              what it took, and once a session that it is idle because nothing
	                              is picked - which is how players find the menu and the command.
	    <exclude block="..."/>    any block the drone must never wrench, for EVERY player - no /das
	                              allow can lift it. Add as many as you like. Names take * as a
	                              wildcard: cntVendingMachine* is every vending machine. Rules players
	                              add in game with /das are kept per player in the SAVE
	                              (droneautomation-salvage.xml) so a mod update cannot lose them.
	-->
	<autoSalvage Radius="4"
	             VerticalRadius="4"
	             SecondsPerStep="1.5"
	             MaxCatchupSeconds="5"
	             LowQualityReach="0.55"
	             LowQualityTimeMult="2"
	             SalvageWorkstations="0"
	             SalvageInPOIs="1"
	             SalvageSwitches="0"
	             SalvageVendingMachines="0"
	             HeatMultiplier="1"
	             ChatPrefix="/das"
	             StartTargets="none"
	             NewTargetPolicy="allow"
	             AnnounceNewTargets="1"
	             CountAsHoldingSalvageTool="1"
	             SalvageToolTags="perkSalvageOperations,salvagingSkill,salvageTool">
		<!-- Examples. Workstations and working vending machines are already covered by
		     SalvageWorkstations="0" and SalvageVendingMachines="0"; use these for anything else you
		     want left standing. -->
		<!-- <exclude block="cntBackpack"/> -->
	</autoSalvage>

	<!--
	  Auto-Harvest: reap and replant grown crops in your own land claim, into the drone's bag.
	    Radius / VerticalRadius   reach over your farm.
	    SecondsPerTarget          charged per crop harvested.
	-->
	<autoHarvest Radius="6"
	             VerticalRadius="4"
	             SecondsPerTarget="1"
	             MaxCatchupSeconds="5"
	             LowQualityReach="0.55"
	             LowQualityTimeMult="2" />

	<!--
	  Auto-Repair: repair damaged blocks in your own land claim, paying mats from the drone's bag.
	    Radius / VerticalRadius   reach over your base.
	    SecondsPerBlock           charged per block fully repaired.
	-->
	<autoRepair Radius="6"
	            VerticalRadius="5"
	            SecondsPerBlock="1"
	            MaxCatchupSeconds="5"
	            LowQualityReach="0.55"
	            LowQualityTimeMult="2" />

	<!--
	  Auto-Plant: sow young crop blocks from the drone's bag onto empty farm plots in your claim.
	  Pairs with Auto-Harvest (which deposits the young "seed" blocks) for a self-running farm.
	    Radius / VerticalRadius   reach over your farm.
	    SecondsPerPlant           charged per crop planted.
	-->
	<autoPlant Radius="6"
	           VerticalRadius="3"
	           SecondsPerPlant="1"
	           MaxCatchupSeconds="5"
	           LowQualityReach="0.55"
	           LowQualityTimeMult="2" />

	<!--
	  Auto-Defense: the drone fires its own machine gun at the nearest hostile it can hit, as a
	  bodyguard while following you or a sentry over the spot you park it on, and turns to face what
	  it is shooting (from 0.13.0; before that it only saw the half of the world facing you). Kills
	  credit you; it never targets you, your allies, party members or traders. Works regardless of the
	  parking/near-owner rules above (a sentry is meant to fight even when you're away) and keeps
	  firing while you have its bag open.
	  Per-shot damage is set on the module itself (item_modifiers.xml); Quality scales these:
	    Range               engagement reach in metres. The drone gun tops out at 15m, so past that
	                        is wasted; this is the Q6 ceiling, scaled down toward Q1 by LowQualityReach.
	    SecondsPerShot      Q6 (fastest) time banked per shot; Q1 is LowQualityTimeMult times slower.
	    MaxCatchupSeconds   ceiling on banked shots, so it can't unload a stored burst on the first
	                        enemy to wander up. Kept small for that reason.
	    RequireLineOfSight  1 = only fire on a clear shot, and pass over a zombie in cover for the
	                        nearest one in the open (the drone gun does no block damage, so this only
	                        saves wasted ammo into cover; 0 fires the instant an enemy is in range).
	    RequireAmmo         1 = every shot spends one round, loaded from the drone's own bag (on from
	                        0.11.0). 0 = the free gun of earlier versions. The drone fires from a
	                        magazine and refills it from the bag only while the bag is closed, so it
	                        keeps shooting while you have its storage open. It says in chat when it
	                        loads its last magazine and when it runs dry; the talk menu shows plenty /
	                        low / empty, and /das ammo gives exact counts.
	    AmmoItems           what it loads, spent in this order. These are the three vanilla's own drone
	                        gun was written to take (Robotic Turret Ammo, Shells and AP); every kind
	                        fires the same round, so the cheap one goes first.
	    MagazineSize        rounds per magazine. 0 = the drone's own (62 on a Q1 drone, up to 92 on Q6).
	    ReloadSeconds       how long a reload takes. The gun falls silent this long when the magazine
	                        runs dry mid-fight; between fights it tops up once nothing has been in its
	                        sights for this long.
	    HeatMultiplier      heat (screamer) per shot, as a multiple of a vanilla auto turret's shot.
	                        1 = the same heat as a turret, 0 = silent, the way versions before 0.11.0
	                        were (the AI director never heard the drone gun at all).
	-->
	<autoDefense Range="15"
	             SecondsPerShot="0.4"
	             MaxCatchupSeconds="2"
	             LowQualityReach="0.6"
	             LowQualityTimeMult="2"
	             RequireLineOfSight="1"
	             RequireAmmo="1"
	             AmmoItems="ammoJunkTurretRegular,ammoJunkTurretShell,ammoJunkTurretAP"
	             MagazineSize="0"
	             ReloadSeconds="3.9"
	             HeatMultiplier="1" />

	<!--
	  Enhancement meta-modules: no automation of their own, they scale EVERY installed core.
	  Each is itself Quality 1-6; the two knobs below are the Q1 and Q6 ends of that scaling.

	  Overclock: cuts every core's per-action time (faster). Multipliers are in (0,1]; lower = faster.
	    Q1TimeMult   action-time multiplier at Quality 1 (weakest overclock).
	    Q6TimeMult   action-time multiplier at Quality 6 (strongest; must be <= Q1TimeMult).
	-->
	<overclock Q1TimeMult="0.85" Q6TimeMult="0.5" />

	<!--
	  Antenna: widens every core's reach (horizontal + vertical). Multipliers are >=1; higher = farther.
	    Q1ReachMult  reach multiplier at Quality 1 (weakest antenna).
	    Q6ReachMult  reach multiplier at Quality 6 (strongest; must be >= Q1ReachMult).
	-->
	<antenna Q1ReachMult="1.15" Q6ReachMult="1.6" />

	<!--
	  Patrol: talk to the drone, "Patrol around me". It roams around you, and with Auto-Defense fitted
	  (switched on, with rounds) it goes after any hostile it can see, closes in and shoots it, then
	  goes back to roaming. Without Auto-Defense it only roams, and comes back to you when a hostile
	  shows up. Not a module: any drone does it. "Stop patrolling" on the same page turns it off; it
	  starts off. The drone stays on Follow, so the teleport back to you and the teleport along with
	  you work as normal. It holds still while you have its menu or bag open, stops while you ride a
	  vehicle or swim, and does not go looking for fights while you crouch. It does not pathfind: it
	  only flies to spots it has a clear line to, and only chases what it can see.
	    Radius          farthest a roam spot may be from you, in metres (at most 28).
	    MinRadius       nearest a roam spot may be to you.
	    PauseSeconds    how long it hovers at each spot before flying to the next.
	    SpeedMult       flying speed while roaming, as a fraction of the drone's own.
	    HoverHeight     how high over the ground it roams, in metres.
	    Hunt            1 = go after hostiles it spots (needs Auto-Defense); 0 = only roam.
	    ChaseRadius     farthest from you it will chase something, in metres. At most 30: vanilla
	                    teleports a following drone back to you at 32 m.
	    StandOff        how far from its target it stops to shoot (kept inside Auto-Defense's reach).
	    ChaseSpeedMult  flying speed while chasing, as a fraction of the drone's own.
	-->
	<patrol Radius="20" MinRadius="5" PauseSeconds="2" SpeedMult="0.5" HoverHeight="2.5" Hunt="1" ChaseRadius="28" StandOff="6" ChaseSpeedMult="1" />
</droneautomation>
